# Skill: status

Cursor adapter for the `status` skill. Full procedure (single source of truth):
`.claude/skills/status/SKILL.md` in this repo, with a read-only gatherer at
`.claude/skills/status/scripts/gather-status.sh`.

## When To Use

The user wants a snapshot of where things stand. This repo has one focus: finishing the HESS paper.

## When Not To Use

Dependency audits, test runs, or deep analysis — those are separate.

## Workflow

Run the gatherer (or equivalent commands) to collect: parent-repo git branch + uncommitted changes,
recent commits, and the `paper/overleaf` nested-repo status (`git -C paper/overleaf status -s`,
`git -C paper/overleaf log --oneline -5`). Surface the open task/TodoWrite focus if any.

## Output Handling

A concise dashboard under ~40 lines: branch, uncommitted, manuscript state, recent commits, current
focus, and 1-3 contextual suggested actions. No box art; use markdown tables.

## Safety Constraints

Strictly read-only — modify no files. Use actual gathered data, not templates.
